From 38483ba7b4c5ef0590e0e4b7cf740d301afabef9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:22:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 238/274] V2 runner: exclude vocabulary padding from
 selected-token ranks

The original Triton rank scan pads to 8192 columns with -inf and counts
padding when the scored token also has logit -inf. On DS41F this reports
131072 instead of 129280. The first TileLang port deliberately preserved
that result to establish reference equivalence.

Now count only columns inside the real vocabulary. This is a separate
correction after the bit-identical port: ties, NaNs and finite selected
logits retain their previous ranks. Token IDs, scores and probabilities are
unchanged. Rank reporting runs after token selection, including trace
replay, and sink recovery copies ranks only as output metadata.

The regression uses DS41F's actual vocabulary through compute_topk_scores
for all three logit types, requires the corrected rank, reproduces the
reference's overcount, and checks that the token IDs and -inf score stay
the same. Nonfinite tests now compare to an independent real-vocabulary
count and document the exact old-reference difference.

Base: local rank port 57b48408fd39ea933c8d7d52d8ce9b69fafc70c0.
Upstream status: local DS41F experiment, not submitted upstream.
Validation: 27 GPU tests pass on DGX4 in candidate-4's image; all 27 also
pass under CUDA 13.0 memcheck, zero errors. All 15 paired performance cases
pass the unchanged gate; FP32 one row 7.79 vs 17.10 us, sixteen rows 8.42
vs 17.45 us, 96 rows 167.99 vs 168.52 us. Offline SM121a compilation, Ruff
and whitespace checks pass. No production promotion.

